    <div class="reveal">
      <h2>The Guildford SEO Landscape</h2>

      <p>Search behaviour differs by type of business. A solicitor on Castle Street needs to rank for "solicitor guildford" in the local pack. A SaaS company at Surrey Research Park needs to rank for industry terms nationally. A restaurant near the Yvonne Arnaud Theatre needs to appear in "near me" searches from theatregoers making last-minute decisions. One generic approach to SEO does not suit all of these, so I plan each business separately.</p>

      <p>AI search adds another channel. Google AI Overviews now appear for many local queries, while ChatGPT and Perplexity are becoming meaningful discovery tools for high-consideration purchases. Businesses that ignore AI search risk losing ground to competitors who prepare for it.</p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="reveal">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

